            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Nice! Couple of observations:\r\n\r\n- All the code from `local set_default_hl` up to (not including) `local _, count` is better moved to an outer scope (for example, before defining section function).\r\n- The `count` computation behind `pcall()` is not really necessary. I'd just use `local count = vim.b.coc_diagnostic_info or {}`.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Nice! Couple of observations:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>All the code from <code class=\"notranslate\">local set_default_hl</code> up to (not including) <code class=\"notranslate\">local _, count</code> is better moved to an outer scope (for example, before defining section function).</li>\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">count</code> computation behind <code class=\"notranslate\">pcall()</code> is not really necessary. I'd just use <code class=\"notranslate\">local count = vim.b.coc_diagnostic_info or {}</code>.</li>\n</ul>",
            "bodyText": "Nice! Couple of observations:\n\nAll the code from local set_default_hl up to (not including) local _, count is better moved to an outer scope (for example, before defining section function).\nThe count computation behind pcall() is not really necessary. I'd just use local count = vim.b.coc_diagnostic_info or {}.",
